  message: "Cross-ref backfill (2026-05-30, deeper-issue investigation): shares the \"output format assumes a smaller dataset than reality delivers\" mechanic with INV-modor (sketch_precomputed.readme_description truncated at 207 chars mid-sentence). Both surface the absence of a data-aware display contract — neither cli.py:3608-3621 (symbols numeric columns) nor the README extractor passes the data's actual range/length distribution to its formatter. Code reference confirmed: In/Out/Deg columns at cli.py:3614-3616 have no min_width; only Kind at 3613 uses a data-driven width. Suggest the structural fix is to compute min_width per numeric column from max(int) digit-count before Rich rendering."  # 0c2d
